// Verify that established connections drop a segment without the ACK flag set.
// Adapted from google/packetdrill commit 83f72d3f9085d0e26eb4d206fe4d7cfab5b6d872,
// gtests/net/tcp/validate/validate-established-no-flags.pkt (GPL-2.0-or-later: the
// repository's LICENSE is GPLv2 and its sources grant "any later version"). Changes for
// Zhida's packet-only runner, tap-echo being the application
// (README "Upstream suites"):
// - defaults.sh (Linux sysctls) and socket/setsockopt/bind/listen/accept dropped: tap-echo
//   listens on port 8080 and accepts.
// - The SYN-ACK's options are written in Zhida's encoding, <mss 1460,sackOK,eol,eol>
//   (Linux: <mss 1460,nop,nop,sackOK>); same options.
// - ioctl(SIOCINQ) = 0 after the segment without flags: nothing was queued for the
//   application, so tap-echo echoes nothing; had it been queued, its echo would come at
//   once and miss the next expectation by 10 ms.
// - ioctl(SIOCINQ) = 1000 after the same bytes with ACK: tap-echo reads and echoes them;
//   the echo carries the ACK of the 1000 bytes.

0    < S 0:0(0) win 20000 <mss 1000,sackOK,nop,nop>
+0   > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 <mss 1460,sackOK,eol,eol>
+.01 < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 20000

+.01 < - 1:1001(1000) win 20000

+.01 < . 1:1001(1000) ack 1 win 20000
+0   > P. 1:1001(1000) ack 1001
